                <pb facs="0246" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/23766: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vera Cruz</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Foster</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-29T12:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">April 29,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 7:16 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>British consul requests to be informed as to whether or not American warships are
                    to be sent to Vera Cruz, for the information of British Admiralty.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foster</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
